# =============================================================
# AOUN PROJECT — ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES TEMPLATE (SAFE TO COMMIT)
# =============================================================
# This file contains NO secrets — only placeholder values + docs.
# Copy it to .env.local and fill in the REAL values:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# ╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  ⛔ NEVER commit .env.local / .env.production            ║
# ║  They are gitignored and contain real secrets.            ║
# ║  .env.example is safe to commit — keep it secret-free!   ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
# =============================================================

# ─── REQUIRED: Server-only secrets & URLs ──────────────────
# These are NEVER sent to the browser. The client only talks
# to /api/proxy — the real backend URL stays on the server.

# .NET Backend API — server-only (NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix!)
# Production example: https://aounn.runasp.net
# Local dev example: http://127.0.0.1:5204
API_URL=https://aounn.runasp.net

# AI/Python backend — server-only (NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix!)
AI_API_URL=https://muhammadmahmoud-awn-ai-service.hf.space

# Optional API key for AI backend — server-only.
# Leave empty if your AI service doesn't require auth.
# AI_API_KEY=

# JWT signing secret — MUST be >= 32 chars, random, never committed.
# Generate:  openssl rand -base64 32
# Or:        node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
JWT_SECRET=CHANGE_ME__GENERATE_A_RANDOM_32_CHAR_SECRET__DO_NOT_COMMIT

# ─── App URL (for sitemap, robots, emails, OpenGraph) ──────
# Server-only canonical URL of THIS Next.js app.
# In production your hosting provider may set NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL;
# Prefer APP_URL (server-only) and keep NEXT_PUBLIC_ only if you
# truly need it on the client (rare).
APP_URL=https://aounn.runasp.net
# SITE_URL is an alias — either works. Kept for backwards compat.
SITE_URL=https://aounn.runasp.net
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL is the ONLY public var allowed — and it must
# be the same value as APP_URL if both are set.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://aounn.runasp.net

# ─── Runtime ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Values: development | test | production
# Next.js sets NODE_ENV automatically for build/start — you rarely
# need to set it manually in .env.local (leave unset for dev).
NODE_ENV=development

# ─── Optional / Dev-only ────────────────────────────────────
# Allow Secure: false cookies over HTTP (local dev only, NEVER prod)
# ALLOW_INSECURE_COOKIES=true

# ─── DEPLOYMENT NOTES ──────────────────────────────────────
# Production (Vercel / RunAsp / Docker):
#   - Do NOT upload .env.local. Instead set env vars in your
#     host's dashboard (Vercel Environment Variables / Docker secrets).
#   - Ensure API_URL uses https in production.
#   - Ensure JWT_SECRET matches the .NET backend's signing key.
#   - Set APP_URL to your production domain.
# Local development:
#   - API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5204 (your local .NET API)
#   - AI_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000 or HF Space URL
#   - APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
#   - ALLOW_INSECURE_COOKIES=true if not using https locally
